  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the type of triangle**: $\\triangle ABD$ is a right triangle with $AB = 13\\text{ cm}$ and $AD = 5\\text{ cm}$.\n2. **Apply the Pythagorean theorem to $\\triangle ABD$**:\n   \\[\n   BD^2 = AB^2 - AD^2 = 13^2 - 5^2 = 169 - 25 = 144\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   BD = \\sqrt{144} = 12\\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n3. **Apply the Pythagorean theorem to $\\triangle BDC$**:\n   \\[\n   BC^2 = BD^2 + DC^2 = 12^2 + 20^2 = 144 + 400 = 544\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   BC = \\sqrt{544} \\approx 23.32\\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n4. **Round BC to the nearest tenth of a centimeter**:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{23.3\\text{ cm}}\n   \\]",
